ENGLISH VERSION
================================================================

Article 1 — Definitions

In this license, the following terms have the meanings set forth
below:

1.1. "CDB" refers to the CodeDashBoard software, including its
     source code, binaries, documentation, configuration files,
     and any derivative work as defined in Article 6.

1.2. "Licensor" refers to Éric Boucher (SIEB), holder of the
     copyright in CDB.

1.3. "User" refers to any natural or legal person who uses, copies,
     modifies, or distributes CDB or a Derivative Product.

1.4. "Derivative Code" refers to any modification, adaptation,
     translation, or extension made to the source code of CDB.

1.5. "Derivative Product" refers to any product, service, or work,
     in whole or in part, that incorporates, includes, or is derived
     from CDB or Derivative Code.

1.6. "CDB Share" refers to the ratio between the number of lines of
     source code (LoC) originating from CDB or Derivative Code and
     the total number of source code lines in the Derivative Product.
     Blank lines and comments are excluded from the calculation.
     The count is performed using a standard line-counting tool (e.g.
     cloc). In case of a disagreement on the method, the method
     chosen by the Licensor prevails.

1.7. "CDB Revenue" refers to any gross revenue directly related to
     CDB, including but not limited to:

     (a) technical support, training, troubleshooting, or
         assistance to users of CDB;
     (b) development work, modification, customization, or
         integration of CDB for a third party, including the
         remuneration, salary, or any other gain derived from such
         work;
     (c) operation of an online service (SaaS) or any other service
         based on CDB;
     (d) sale or commercial distribution of a Derivative Product
         whose CDB Share is equal to or greater than 10%.

1.8. "Royalty" refers to the amount owed to the Licensor under
     Article 4.

Article 2 — Grant of Rights

Subject to compliance with all terms of this license, the Licensor
grants to any User the non-exclusive, worldwide, and perpetual right
to use, copy, modify, and distribute CDB, including for commercial
purposes.

Article 3 — Tool Usage Exemption

The use of CDB as a development tool — notably as an integrated
development environment — to create, develop, or maintain software
that does not incorporate CDB code does not constitute usage subject
to the Royalty. This exemption covers internal corporate use,
personal use, and educational use.

Article 4 — Royalty

4.1. Any User who derives CDB Revenue shall pay the Licensor a
     Royalty equal to 10% of the gross revenue of CDB Revenue. This
     Royalty is due from the first dollar, with no threshold or
     exemption.

4.2. With respect to CDB Revenue under paragraph 1.7(d) (sale or
     distribution of a Derivative Product), the Royalty applies
     only if the CDB Share of the Derivative Product is equal to or
     greater than 10%. Once this threshold is met, the Royalty is
     10% of the gross revenue of that Derivative Product.

4.3. CDB Revenue under paragraphs 1.7(a), (b), and (c) is subject
     to the Royalty without any threshold condition.

4.4. The Royalty is payable within 30 days of the User becoming
     aware of the obligation to pay the Royalty. The Licensor
     provides payment instructions upon request.

Article 5 — Attribution

Any distribution of CDB or Derivative Code, as well as any
Derivative Product, must include a visible notice of the copyright
holder and of this license, in accordance with the following
wording:

  "This product includes code from CodeDashBoard (CDB),
   Copyright (c) 2026 Éric Boucher (SIEB) <eb@sieb.ca>"

Article 6 — Modifications and Derivative Code

The User may modify CDB and keep modifications private (no
obligation to publish source code). Any modification remains subject
to this license, including the attribution requirement (Article 5)
and the Royalty (Article 4).

Article 7 — Compliance and Enforcement

7.1. Declaration: any User subject to the Royalty shall, upon
     request by the Licensor, provide a declaration of CDB Revenue
     received.

7.2. Audit: the Licensor reserves the right to verify the compliance
     of any User, including examination of the source code of
     Derivative Products (for the purpose of calculating the CDB
     Share) and review of accounting records related to CDB Revenue.
     Such audit may be conducted at reasonable intervals and upon
     14 days' notice.

7.3. The Licensor may exercise any legal means available to enforce
     this license, including legal proceedings, without this
     enumeration being limiting.

Article 8 — No Warranty

CDB is provided "as is", without any warranty of any kind, express or
implied, including without limitation the warranties of
merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and
non-infringement. The Licensor does not warrant that CDB will be
error-free or that its use will be uninterrupted.

Article 9 — Limitation of Liability

In no event shall the Licensor be liable for any direct, indirect,
incidental, special, or consequential damages arising from the use
or inability to use CDB. The total liability of the Licensor is
capped at the amount actually received from the User for CDB, or
zero if CDB was obtained free of charge.

Article 10 — Termination

Failure to comply with any term of this license, including failure
to pay the Royalty, results in the immediate and automatic
termination of the right to use CDB. Upon termination, the User
must cease all use and distribution of CDB and any Derivative
Product, and destroy all copies in their possession.

Article 11 — General Provisions

11.1. Governing law: this license is governed by the laws in force
      in Québec, Canada.

11.2. Severability: if any provision of this license is held to be
      invalid or unenforceable, the remaining provisions remain in
      effect.

11.3. Entire agreement: this license constitutes the entire
      agreement between the Licensor and the User regarding CDB.

11.4. Amendment: any amendment to this license must be in writing
      and signed by the Licensor.

11.5. Trademarks: this license does not grant any right to use the
      trademarks, trade names, or logos of the Licensor, including
      "SIEB", "CodeDashBoard", and "CDB".

